# Copy to .env (install.sh does this). Only what must exist before configuration can be read, and the dashboard's own
# access controls, live here. Every operator setting and every credential lives in the settings store (data/store/), edited on
# the dashboard's Settings screen or with the mise run config:* tasks. No credential belongs in this file. An edit to this file
# applies when the containers are created or the dashboard is started again.

# --- compose ---------------------------------------------------------------
# install.sh sets this to include the GPU overlay when an NVIDIA GPU is present.
COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml
# Optional services to start with the stack: `eyes` (vision), `ears` (listens), `mouth` (speaks) and `discord` (the Discord
# connector that carries the voice channel to and from them). Listing them here keeps them on across restarts and Launch.
# The Discord ones need the bot token (connections.discord.token) and the guild and channel ids set in the settings.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=discord,ears,mouth
# The optional speech engine servers take profiles the same way: `pocket` (voice.engine pocket), `nemotron` and `kyutai`
# (ears.stt_engine nemotron or kyutai). Each is built on first use, which takes minutes.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=pocket,nemotron,kyutai
# GPU: COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.gpu.yml. A Windows docker.exe (COHOST_DOCKER_BIN below) splits
# that list on `;`, so also set COMPOSE_PATH_SEPARATOR to `:` in that case.
# Override the TTS / STT images (the GPU overlay switches them to the CUDA builds by default).
# KOKORO_IMAGE=ghcr.io/remsky/kokoro-fastapi-cpu:v0.10.0
# @spec DEPLOY-ENG-017
# The GPU overlay runs Kokoro's CUDA 12.8 build, which RTX 50-series cards need and which needs an NVIDIA driver of the
# R570 series or newer. On a GTX 9xx/10xx card, an older driver or an arm64 host, or if the tts container will not start,
# use the CUDA 12.6 build instead:
# KOKORO_IMAGE=ghcr.io/remsky/kokoro-fastapi-gpu:v0.10.0-cu126
# SPEACHES_IMAGE=ghcr.io/speaches-ai/speaches:0.8.3-cpu

# --- Host-run dashboard (`mise run dashboard`) -------------------------------------
# The dashboard runs on the host, not in Compose; its Launch button starts the stack. Its ports are the settings dashboard.port and
# dashboard.lan_port (edit them on the Settings screen).
# Where the full surface listens. 127.0.0.1 = this machine only. 0.0.0.0 opens the full dashboard to other machines,
# and the control token and the unlock cookie then cross the network in cleartext (plain HTTP).
# That is the way to reach the dashboard from another machine: never put a port forward or proxy in front of the
# loopback port. An ssh -L tunnel from your own machine is fine.
DASHBOARD_HOST=127.0.0.1
# The control token, cohost's one lock, is not set here: mise run config:token sets it (install.sh runs it once) and prints it
# once for your password manager, and the settings store keeps only its verifier. The dashboard and the control plane refuse
# to start anything while this file defines CONTROL_TOKEN.
# 1 lets the controls also stop and restart redis and postgres (read-only by default).
# CONTROL_ADVANCED=0
# The docker executable the dashboard and cohostctl run. WSL2 without Docker Desktop's WSL integration
# has no `docker` on its PATH: set this to docker.exe.
# COHOST_DOCKER_BIN=docker.exe

# --- Service health ----------------------------------------------------------
# How often each service publishes its heartbeat (ms). Dashboard "services" tab
# and the compose healthchecks derive staleness from this.
# HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS=5000

# --- Files ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where services keep files they must remember across restarts (refreshed Twitch tokens, the fallback clip cache).
# Unset = `data/` under the repository root.
# COHOST_DATA_DIR=
# The settings store's master key file. Unset = ~/.config/cohost/master.key (outside the checkout, so a copy of the checkout
# or of data/ carries no key). Keep the recovery key it was shown with in your password manager.
# COHOST_KEY_FILE=

